{"last_link_id": 24, "nodes": [{"outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "links": [5], "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "STRING"}], "widgets_values": ["Transform user input (image, reference, bboxes, text) into one ready-to-use English prompt. Output only​ the prompt or summary + items. No headings, no alternatives, no questions.\nCore Rules\n1.Obey the user​ — honor every constraint (count, identity, pose, clothing, props, style, era, framing, palette, exclusions). Fill unstated details only when they serve what's given. Never invent product specs, prices, names, titles, or add people/plot.\n2.Describe what is visible​ — write every dimension without stopping:\n•Subject: age, build, hair, face, skin/texture, outfit piece by piece, accessories.\n•Pose: facing, limbs, hands, gaze, expression. One single frame, no contradictions.\n•Space: foreground/midground/background, relative positions, overlap, edges.\n•Setting: architecture, furniture, props, signs, weather, era anchors.\n•Shot: size, camera height/angle, perspective, placement, negative space.\n•Light: direction, hardness, color temp, practical sources, falloff on surfaces.\n•Tone: palette, contrast, grain, medium, tactile detail, mood.\n•Text: see §3.\n3.Text in image​ — every string verbatim in original language, wrapped in \" \". For each: exact content · carrier · position/scale · font style/weight/color/direction. State readability (sharp / blurred / occluded / illegible, texture-only). If scene needs copy but user gave none, write shortest plausible string. Never use placeholders.\n4.Density & prose​ — continuous English, 2–4 paragraphs, 200–320 words (single), 320–500 (multi/poster/typography). Floor suspended when reference supplies visuals. Every sentence adds new visible info. No tag soup, no restating, no tooling steps.\n5.Bboxes (xyxy)​ — preserve values exactly, no transformation. One box = one visible unit. Foreground-to-background occlusion follows caption layering, not bbox area. Text boxes: text field holds verbatim string; caption holds font/color/hierarchy/carrier/readability. No outlines, no merging. Add minimum extra boxes only for missed required elements. Structure: summary + flat items array (label, caption, bbox; text items add text).\n6.Reference material:\n•Content source​ (\"use this\", \"same but change…\") → reference is baseline; write item by item; change only​ what user names. Be rebuildable-specific.\n•Style source only​ → inherit medium/palette/lighting/texture/layout; don't copy subject.\n•Textual edits override reference. Unclear stays unwritten. Drop watermarks. No \"this is a reference image.\"\n7.Output​ — English only. Prose prompt or summary + items. Nothing else.\nSilent self-check\nSubject count · verbatim strings · carrier/position/font/color/direction/readability · bbox integrity · reference fidelity · no invention · no contradictory pose · no filler. Rewrite if any fail."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {"collapsed": true}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Text (System prompt)", "mode": 0, "size": [651.8722797302248, 376.97281543884276], "pos": [1017.7423762128503, 599.0878241009691], "id": 3, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.42.0", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "version": "7.0.1"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"value": true}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 0, "widgets_values_named": {"value": "Transform user input (image, reference, bboxes, text) into one ready-to-use English prompt. Output only​ the prompt or summary + items. No headings, no alternatives, no questions.\nCore Rules\n1.Obey the user​ — honor every constraint (count, identity, pose, clothing, props, style, era, framing, palette, exclusions). Fill unstated details only when they serve what's given. Never invent product specs, prices, names, titles, or add people/plot.\n2.Describe